    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ACS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " an LMWH, UFH or bivalirudin = given routinely unless contraindicated. Enoxaparin = an alt to UFH in NSTE-ACS when an early invasive strategy isn't planned, and = the recommended anticoag w fibrinolysis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "UFH w a fibrinolytic in STEMI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 60 units/kg IV bolus (max 4000 units), then 12 units/kg/h (max 1000 units/h) for 48 h or until PCI = complete. Enoxaparin: UA/NSTEMI 1 mg/kg SC every 12 h w ASA; STEMI 30 mg IV bolus plus 1 mg/kg SC, then 1 mg/kg SC every 12 h, w a lower dose @ ≥ 75 years."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "PLT:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " check b4 and periodically during heparin; thrombocytopenia occurs in up to 30%, 2–20 days (avg 5–9) after starting. If PLT fall below 100,000 or thrombosis recurs, stop heparin and evaluate for HIT; HIT can occur up to several wks after heparin = stopped."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Enoxaparin w CrCl < 30 mL/min:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tx doses become 1 mg/kg SC QD."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning (LMWH):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " epidural or spinal hematomas w neuraxial anesthesia or spinal puncture, which may cause long-term or permanent paralysis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Protamine dosing:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " each mg neutralizes about 100 units of UFH, ⍉more than 50 mg in any 10 minutes, given very slowly; for enoxaparin, 1 mg per 1 mg, and anti-Xa activity = never fully neutralized (max about 60%)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
